1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,525
Your CPU might have 8 cores.

2
00:00:02,805 --> 00:00:04,760
Your graphics card has thousands.

3
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:07,419
So why isn't the GPU in charge?

4
00:00:08,169 --> 00:00:11,414
CPU cores are like a few expert workers.

5
00:00:11,694 --> 00:00:16,724
Each one is fast and clever, and great at complicated, step-by-step jobs.

6
00:00:17,474 --> 00:00:20,937
GPU cores are a huge crowd of simpler workers.

7
00:00:21,217 --> 00:00:23,072
On their own, they're not that smart.

8
00:00:23,822 --> 00:00:29,022
But a frame is millions of pixels, and most of them can be worked out at the same time.

9
00:00:29,302 --> 00:00:33,516
Give each worker a few pixels, and the whole picture fills in at once.

10
00:00:34,266 --> 00:00:40,282
That's why games lean on the GPU for frame rate, while the CPU runs everything else.

11
00:00:40,562 --> 00:00:44,828
See every part of your PC explained in the full video on the channel.

